  "description": "Erection of a 4.5m deep single-storey rear extension with a crown roof (2.9m eaves / 3.96m ridge) utilizing reclaimed brick, matching render, and red clay tiles. Works include the removal of the existing conservatory and north chimney stack; the conversion of theexisting garage to an art studio with new window insertions; and the replacement of pebble dash with light grey render. Fenestration changes include the removal of one large rooflight and the installation of three new units (two 0.9m x 0.9m to west/south and one 1.8m x 0.9m obscure-glazed to north); the installation of triple/vacuum windows/glazing; and an external air source heat pump. The project includes a full roof renovation with upgraded insulation and the provision of a front garden turning area. Landscaping involves fencing renovation and the removal of five low-value trees (one for development, four for arboricultural reasons) to be mitigated by native, climate-resilient replanting.",
